Package: tor-control-panel-common
Architecture: all
## bash (>= 4.4): the privileged helpers and the libexec wrappers open with
## 'shopt -s inherit_errexit', which does not exist before 4.4 -- an older
## /bin/bash fails in the preamble instead of running the script.
Depends: bash (>= 4.4),
         helper-scripts,
         python3,
         safe-rm,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: privleap | tor-control-panel-pkexec
Description: Tor control panel - GUI-independent config logic and helpers
 The configuration logic shared by tor-control-panel and anon-connection-wizard,
 with NO GUI (PyQt) dependency: torrc generation and parsing, DisableNetwork
 handling, input validation, and the privilege runner. Ships the privileged
 helpers that write the torrc, control the Tor service and make the torrc sane,
 plus the default-bridge data.
 .
 The privileged helpers run via privleap's leaprun on Whonix / Kicksecure, or
 via pkexec (the tor-control-panel-pkexec package) or passwordless sudo on plain
 Debian; hence the escalators are Recommends, not hard dependencies.
 .
 Installing this package alone lets the Tor configuration code be used from the
 command line, without pulling in PyQt. The graphical front-ends are in the
 tor-control-panel package.

Package: tor-control-panel-pkexec
Architecture: all
Depends: tor-control-panel-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         polkitd,
         pkexec,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: mate-polkit
Description: Tor control panel - pkexec/polkit privilege policies
 The PolicyKit action files that let tor-control-panel escalate privilege via
 pkexec on systems without privleap (plain Debian). Each action authorizes one
 fixed, self-validating helper: control the tor@default service, stage the
 torrc, make the torrc sane, and read the Tor log.
 .
 Not needed on Whonix / Kicksecure, where privleap is used instead.

Package: tor-control-panel
Architecture: all
Depends: tor-control-panel-common (= ${binary:Version}),
         python3,
         python3-pyqt5,
         python3-stem,
         python3-yaml,
         qtwayland5,
